"class":267,"line":395},[265,1029,1030],{"class":279},"host",[265,1032,596],{"class":275},[265,1034,865],{"class":279},[265,1036,596],{"class":275},[265,1038,1039],{"class":318},"register",[265,1041,1042],{"class":279},"(identifier",[265,1044,283],{"class":275},[265,1046,916],{"class":275},[265,1048,363],{"class":318},[265,1050,1051],{"class":279},"())   ",[265,1053,1054],{"class":587},"\u002F\u002F → srv:\u002F\u002Fapp.acme-org.orders-app~com.example.GreetingService\n",[265,1056,1057],{"class":267,"line":421},[265,1058,309],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":308},[265,1060,1061],{"class":267,"line":427},[265,1062,1063],{"class":587},"\u002F\u002F later, when the service should no longer be reachable\n",[265,1065,1066,1068,1070,1072,1074,1077],{"class":267,"line":432},[265,1067,1030],{"class":279},[265,1069,596],{"class":275},[265,1071,865],{"class":279},[265,1073,596],{"class":275},[265,1075,1076],{"class":318},"unRegister",[265,1078,1079],{"class":279},"(identifier)\n",[239,1081,1082,1083,1085,1086,1089,1090,1092,1093,1095],{},"The zone is the complete zone the service lives in: ",[243,1084,516],{}," and ",[243,1087,1088],{},"defaultZone"," apply to ",[243,1091,245],{}," classes only. Registering the same identifier twice on one client is a no-op, and ",[243,1094,1076],{}," ends any stream the service is still producing with an error to its caller.",[251,1097,1099],{"id":1098},"the-service-directory","The service directory",[239,1101,1102,1103,1106,1107,1085,1110,1113,1114,1117,1118,1121,1122,1124,1125,1128,1129,1132,1133,1136,1137,1139],{},"Every published class under the project's ",[243,1104,1105],{},"servicesPaths"," gets a service definition from ",[243,1108,1109],{},"kinotic generate",[243,1111,1112],{},"kinotic sync",", its functions with their parameters and types, written to the ",[243,1115,1116],{},"ServiceDefinitions"," module under ",[243,1119,1120],{},"generatedPath",". A project that imports that module has the runtime register each service in the platform's service directory as the service comes online: the services registered before ",[243,1123,933],{}," when the client connects, and a service registered on a connected client as it registers. Only a service in an application's zone, ",[243,1126,1127],{},"app.\u003CorganizationId>.\u003CapplicationId>"," or a zone under it, is registered, through the platform's ",[243,1130,1131],{},"ApplicationServiceDirectory"," in ",[243,1134,1135],{},"app-api",", which refuses a zone that is not the application's or an application outside the caller's organization. The directory then holds the application's services beside the platform's own, with their liveness; a service the project declares no definition for serves on its zone alone. A definition naming other functions than the class serves fails the registration, and with it the connection, until ",[243,1138,1112],{}," runs again.",[1141,1142,1144],"h3",{"id":1143},"parameter-and-return-types","Parameter and return types",[239,1146,1147],{},"Arguments and results travel as JSON, so a function's types are published as JSON carries them:",[1149,1150,1151,1167,1177,1198,1207,1220],"ul",{},[1152,1153,1154,1155,1158,1159,1162,1163,1166],"li",{},"A ",[243,1156,1157],{},"Promise"," or ",[243,1160,1161],{},"PromiseLike"," result is asynchronous and an ",[243,1164,1165],{},"Observable"," result is a stream, of the type it resolves to or emits.",[1152,1168,1169,1172,1173,1176],{},[243,1170,1171],{},"any",", ",[243,1174,1175],{},"unknown",", and a type parameter with no constraint accept anything; a constrained type parameter is its constraint.",[1152,1178,1179,1180,1183,1184,1085,1187,1190,1191,1172,1194,1197],{},"Interfaces, classes (their fields, without their methods), generic instantiations such as ",[243,1181,1182],{},"Page\u003CReport>",", mapped types such as ",[243,1185,1186],{},"Partial\u003CReport>",[243,1188,1189],{},"Pick\u003CReport, 'id'>",", intersections, and unions of objects are objects, named for the type and its type arguments (",[243,1192,1193],{},"Page_Report",[243,1195,1196],{},"Partial_Report",").",[1152,1199,1200,1085,1203,1206],{},[243,1201,1202],{},"Record\u003Cstring, V>",[243,1204,1205],{},"{[key: string]: V}"," are maps, enums are enums, and a union of string literals is a string.",[1152,1208,1154,1209,1212,1213,1215,1216,1219],{},[243,1210,1211],{},"Date"," is published as a date, but it arrives as the ISO-8601 string a date travels as: the service receives a string, and a TypeScript caller gets a string back. ",[243,1214,1109],{}," logs a warning for each one, and the directory carries the same warning in the ",[243,1217,1218],{},"warnings"," metadata of the parameter, or of the function for a result.",[1152,1221,1154,1222,1172,1225,1172,1228,1172,1231,1172,1234,1237],{},[243,1223,1224],{},"Map",[243,1226,1227],{},"Set",[243,1229,1230],{},"Uint8Array",[243,1232,1233],{},"Buffer",[243,1235,1236],{},"bigint",", tuple, or function fails generation with the reason and the type to declare instead.",[251,1239,1241],{"id":1240},"decorators","Decorators",[1141,1243,1245],{"id":1244},"publishnamespace-name-advertise","@Publish(namespace?, name?, advertise?)",[239,1247,1248,1249,1252,1253,1256,1257,1260,1261,1264,1265,1268],{},"Marks a class for publication. The full service identifier becomes ",[243,1250,1251],{},"namespace.ClassName","; both parts are optional (the name defaults to the class name). A service published with no namespace is addressed by its name in its zone, ",[243,1254,1255],{},"srv:\u002F\u002F\u003Czone>~ClassName",", and the platform's service directory names it in its zone's namespace, ",[243,1258,1259],{},"\u003Czone>.ClassName",", so services of the same name in different applications stay apart. Passing ",[243,1262,1263],{},"advertise"," as ",[243,1266,1267],{},"true"," additionally advertises the service in the platform service directory, so it appears in directory listings for browsing and invocation — publishing alone makes a service callable over RPC without listing it.",[1141,1270,1272],{"id":1271},"zonezone","@Zone(zone)",[239,1274,1275,1276,1278],{},"Declares the zone the service is addressable in, relative to the client's ",[243,1277,516],{},". The zone is one or more dot-separated labels of lowercase letters, digits, and interior dashes.",[1141,1280,1282],{"id":1281},"versionversion","@Version(version)",[239,1284,1285,1286,1289],{},"Sets the semantic version for the service in ",[243,1287,1288],{},"X.Y.Z"," format. Callers can pin to a specific version when resolving the service.",[1141,1291,1293],{"id":1292},"scope","@Scope",[239,1295,1296],{},"A getter or method decorator that marks the member providing the scope identifier. Scope targets requests at one specific instance of a service — for example the copy running on a particular node or device.",[256,1298,1300],{"className":258,"code":1299,"language":260,"meta":261,"style":261},"import { Publish, Scope } from '@kinotic-ai\u002Fcore'\n\n@Publish('com.example')\nclass DeviceService {\n    deviceId: string\n\n    @Scope\n    get scope(): string {\n        return this.deviceId\n    }\n\n    constructor(deviceId: string) {\n        this.deviceId = deviceId\n    }\n\n    getStatus(): string {\n        return `Status for device ${this.deviceId}`\n    }\n}\n",[243,1301,1302,1325,1329,1345,1354,1364,1368,1376,1391,1401,1405,1409,1428,1441,1446,1451,1463,1483,1488],{"__ignoreMap":261},[265,1303,1304,1306,1308,1310,1312,1315,1317,1319,1321,1323],{"class":267,"line":268},[265,1305,272],{"class":271},[265,1307,276],{"class":275},[265,1309,280],{"class":279},[265,1311,283],{"class":275},[265,1313,1314],{"class":279}," Scope",[265,1316,289],{"class":275},[265,1318,292],{"class":271},[265,1320,295],{"class":275},[265,1322,299],{"class":298},[265,1324,302],{"class":275},[265,1326,1327],{"class":267,"line":305},[265,1328,309],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":308},[265,1330,1331,1333,1335,1337,1339,1341,1343],{"class":267,"line":312},[265,1332,315],{"class":275},[265,1334,341],{"